# Shared "is this release complete?" predicate. BOTH gates in
# build-desktop.yml call it — the version gate judges an already-published
# release, the release job judges the artifacts it just downloaded — so a
# clean clone without it breaks the release pipeline in CI rather than
# locally, which is the worst place to discover a missing file.
!/scripts/release_assets.py
!/scripts/build_native_runtime.py
!/scripts/build_python_wheels.py
# Shared "is this VERSION documented?" predicate. The version gate in
# build-desktop.yml calls it BEFORE any build, so a clean clone without it
# fails the release pipeline in CI — the same worst-place-to-discover argument
# as release_assets.py above. It is also the reason nine versions (0.11.0
# through 0.15.2) shipped with no changelog entry: nothing in the repo
# referenced CHANGELOG.md, so no check could observe the drift.
!/scripts/changelog_gate.py
!/scripts/check_architecture.py
# Cache-waste distribution report. The measurement discipline it encodes —
# rates DERIVED from lib.cost rather than hand-written, non-waste classes
# (TTL expiry / cold start) excluded from the recoverable denominator,
# percentiles that treat 0 as a number — is the deliverable. An untracked copy
# means the next cost audit goes back to throwaway one-liners and re-makes the
# errors tests/cache/test_cache_waste_report.py now pins.
!/scripts/report_tool_search_outcomes.py
!/scripts/cache_waste_report.py
# Second-path cache A/B probe. It is the control the gateway report is missing,
# and it is DRY-RUN by default — the value is the encoded experiment design
# (deterministic prefix, 4k to clear the cacheable minimum cheaply, and the
# size-dependence caveat that stops a cheap null result being read as
# exoneration). An untracked copy means whoever finally runs the control
# re-derives that design and probably drops the caveat.
!/scripts/cache_ab_probe.py
# debug/ = standalone scratch/benchmark scripts (never imported by the app);
# tracked *.log already ignored above, this covers the .py/.json/.png/.md/.html too.
# NOTE: contents-level (/debug/*), NOT dir-level (/debug/) — git never descends
# into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a /debug/ rule would make the negation below
# dead (the uploads/* + !.gitkeep pattern is the established shape).
/debug/*
!/debug/AGENTS.md
# Whitelist: the CI wizard pixel probe (the manual installer-ui-probe.yml
# workflow drives it on windows-latest). That workflow ships in the
# opensource export, so the script must too — the same dead-pipeline
# argument as release_assets.py: a public clone without it carries a
# workflow that dies on a missing file.
!/debug/win_ci_shot.py
# Canonical read-only conversation diagnostic used by serverctl and shipped
# into source/Docker installs; all other debug scripts remain scratch-only.
!/debug/inspect_conversation.py
# Read-only first-attempt tool-call pass-rate report aggregating the
